<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>WJ24 frame-to-kicker joint concepts</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --ink: #1d2a33;
      --muted: #4e5d66;
      --line: #cbd4da;
      --frame: #8fa2ad;
      --frame-dark: #647984;
      --header: #c8d3d9;
      --new: #e9b36e;
      --new-dark: #9b5c16;
      --panel: #d8e7ef;
      --bolt: #173d55;
      --warning: #fff1d8;
      --paper: #f5f7f8;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--paper);
      color: var(--ink);
      font: 16px/1.45 system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    }
    main { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 28px 20px 56px; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.3rem); line-height: 1.12; }
    h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.2; }
    h3 { margin: 0 0 5px; font-size: 1rem; }
    p { margin: 8px 0; }
    .intro { max-width: 78ch; color: var(--muted); }
    .status {
      display: inline-block;
      margin: 12px 0 20px;
      padding: 5px 9px;
      border: 1px solid #d5a357;
      border-radius: 5px;
      background: var(--warning);
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: .86rem;
    }
    .concept {
      margin: 18px 0;
      padding: 18px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 10px;
      background: white;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 2px #18252d0c;
    }
    .concept-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .tag { color: var(--muted); font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 650; }
    .details { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 6px; }
    .details p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .93rem; }
    figure { margin: 13px 0 6px; }
    svg {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      border: 1px solid #e0e5e8;
      border-radius: 7px;
      background: #fbfcfc;
    }
    svg text { fill: var(--ink); font: 12px system-ui, sans-serif; }
    svg .small { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 10px; }
    svg .tiny { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 9px; }
    svg .member { fill: var(--frame); stroke: #526671; stroke-width: 1.5; }
    svg .header { fill: var(--header); stroke: #53656e; stroke-width: 1.5; }
    svg .panel { fill: var(--panel); stroke: #6b8594; stroke-width: 1.5; }
    svg .candidate { fill: var(--new); stroke: var(--new-dark); stroke-width: 1.5; }
    svg .candidate-line { fill: none; stroke: var(--new-dark); stroke-width: 8; stroke-linecap: square; }
    svg .existing-link { fill: none; stroke: var(--frame-dark); stroke-width: 12; stroke-linecap: square; }
    svg .bolt { stroke: var(--bolt); stroke-width: 2.2; fill: none; }
    svg .bolt-head { fill: white; stroke: var(--bolt); stroke-width: 2; }
    svg .bolt-dot { fill: var(--bolt); stroke: none; }
    svg .ghost { fill: none; stroke: #71818a; stroke-width: 1.7; stroke-dasharray: 6 5; }
    svg .leader { stroke: #71818a; stroke-width: 1; fill: none; }
    svg .section-divider { stroke: #d4dce0; stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 4; }
    .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 18px; margin-top: 10px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .84rem; }
    .key { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; }
    .swatch { width: 14px; height: 14px; border: 1px solid #5f6d74; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--frame); }
    .swatch.header { background: var(--header); }
    .swatch.new { background: var(--new); border-color: var(--new-dark); }
    .swatch.panel { background: var(--panel); }
    .axis-key { color: var(--bolt); font-weight: 700; }
    .callout {
      margin: 22px 0;
      padding: 15px 17px;
      border-left: 4px solid #3e718d;
      background: #eaf2f6;
    }
    .callout p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
    .callout p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .open-items { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 20px; }
    .open-items section { padding: 14px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; background: white; }
    ul { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; }
    li + li { margin-top: 5px; }
    .foot { margin-top: 19px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .86rem; }
    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      main { padding: 20px 12px 38px; }
      .concept { padding: 13px; }
      .details, .open-items { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2px; }
      svg text { font-size: 14px; }
      svg .small { font-size: 11px; }
      svg .tiny { font-size: 10px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>WJ24 frame-to-kicker joint concepts</h1>
  <p class="intro">Three side-view sketches compare the current outer and center interfaces with two timber-only development options. The outer frame-to-header tie and the center kicker-backers are separate joint families. The sketches show member relationships and bolt directions only; they are not CAD, shop dimensions, a selected design, or evidence of capacity.</p>
  <span class="status">WJ24 development study · geometry and mechanics open · no cutting or drilling released</span>

  <section class="concept" aria-labelledby="current-title">
    <div class="concept-head"><h2 id="current-title">1. Current WJ24 reference</h2><span class="tag">Outer WJ03 knee plus separate center connections</span></div>
    <figure>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="current-svg-title current-svg-desc">
        <title id="current-svg-title">Current WJ24 outer frame and center header connections</title>
        <desc id="current-svg-desc">At the outer station, a three-piece knee links the sloped base side and outer post to the header. At the center station, separate cleats connect the principal and short post to the header; the kicker backer sits below the header as its own joint.</desc>
        <text x="35" y="25" font-weight="700">OUTER FRAME / HEADER</text>
        <text x="535" y="25" font-weight="700">CENTER PRINCIPAL / POST / BACKER</text>
        <line class="section-divider" x1="500" y1="18" x2="500" y2="280" />
        <!-- Outer view -->
        <rect class="header" x="65" y="171" width="390" height="39" rx="2" />
        <text x="74" y="196">kicker header</text>
        <rect class="member" x="180" y="210" width="64" height="70" />
        <text x="163" y="296" class="small">outer kicker post</text>
        <path class="member" d="M155 171 L190 132 L356 38 L385 77 L219 171 Z" />
        <text x="275" y="55" class="small">outer 4×6 rim</text>
        <path class="existing-link" d="M208 162 L247 119" />
        <rect class="member" x="256" y="113" width="112" height="27" transform="rotate(-30 312 126.5)" />
        <rect class="member" x="105" y="145" width="111" height="25" />
        <rect class="member" x="248" y="210" width="118" height="28" />
        <text x="77" y="127" class="small">rear bridge</text>
        <path class="leader" d="M128 131 L145 146" />
        <text x="263" y="108" class="small">knee spine</text>
        <path class="leader" d="M300 111 L303 119" />
        <text x="251" y="251" class="tiny">under-header link</text>
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="220" cy="132" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-head" cx="235" cy="143" r="4" />
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="293" cy="168" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-head" cx="321" cy="168" r="4" />
        <line class="bolt" x1="366" y1="162" x2="366" y2="207" />
        <path class="bolt" d="M361 200 L366 207 L371 200" />
        <text x="371" y="204" class="tiny">Z</text>
        <text x="82" y="232" class="small">Separate blocks, multiple bolt directions and access faces</text>
        <!-- Center view -->
        <rect class="header" x="555" y="171" width="390" height="39" rx="2" />
        <text x="563" y="196">kicker header</text>
        <rect class="member" x="668" y="210" width="55" height="70" />
        <text x="640" y="296" class="small">center kicker post</text>
        <path class="member" d="M782 171 L819 143 L902 35 L933 71 L850 171 Z" />
        <text x="798" y="48" class="small">center 4×6 principal</text>
        <path class="candidate" d="M704 171 L782 171 L819 143 L741 143 Z" />
        <text x="746" y="135" class="tiny">short upper cleat</text>
        <rect class="candidate" x="640" y="210" width="28" height="40" />
        <text x="630" y="265" class="tiny">post/header seat</text>
        <rect class="member" x="741" y="210" width="72" height="44" />
        <text x="730" y="270" class="tiny">center kicker backer</text>
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="766" cy="155" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="766" cy="155" r="1.5" />
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="781" cy="164" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="781" cy="164" r="1.5" />
        <text x="774" y="128" class="tiny">X pair through principal</text>
        <line class="bolt" x1="739" y1="143" x2="739" y2="211" /><path class="bolt" d="M734 204 L739 211 L744 204" />
        <text x="829" y="199" class="tiny">Z pair into header</text>
        <text x="564" y="248" class="small">Backer has its own under-header seat and fasteners</text>
      </svg>
      <div class="legend" aria-label="Diagram legend">
        <span class="key"><span class="swatch"></span>Existing frame timber</span>
        <span class="key"><span class="swatch header"></span>Header</span>
        <span class="key"><span class="swatch new"></span>Existing candidate cleat</span>
        <span class="key"><span class="axis-key">Z ↓ / X ⊙</span>Illustrative bolt axis; tool access remains open</span>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <div class="details">
      <p><strong>Outer family.</strong> The outer 4×6 rim and kicker post connect to the shared header through a knee spine, rear bridge, and under-header link. The three-piece detour is the part being simplified.</p>
      <p><strong>Center family.</strong> Separate cleats connect the center principal and kicker post to the header. The center kicker backer remains below the header as its own receiver, with separate kicker screws and provisional header bolts.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="concept" aria-labelledby="overall-title">
    <div class="concept-head"><h2 id="overall-title">2. Overall option: deeper header with direct timber seats</h2><span class="tag">Preferred concept to compare in the viewer; not selected</span></div>
    <figure>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 310" role="img" aria-labelledby="overall-svg-title overall-svg-desc">
        <title id="overall-svg-title">Deeper header with simpler outer and center timber seats</title>
        <desc id="overall-svg-desc">A deeper header keeps its current front and top datums and extends rearward. Simple timber blocks replace the outer knee, and a full-section block sits between the center principal and header. Separate under-header seats support the kicker posts and separate backers.</desc>
        <text x="35" y="25" font-weight="700">OUTER: SIMPLE UPPER + LOWER SEATS</text>
        <text x="535" y="25" font-weight="700">CENTER: FULL-SECTION PRINCIPAL BLOCK</text>
        <line class="section-divider" x1="500" y1="18" x2="500" y2="286" />
        <!-- Outer view -->
        <rect class="header" x="59" y="171" width="418" height="40" rx="2" />
        <rect class="ghost" x="59" y="171" width="72" height="40" />
        <text x="66" y="196">kicker header</text>
        <text x="64" y="224" class="tiny">rearward depth trial →</text>
        <rect class="member" x="180" y="211" width="64" height="70" />
        <text x="152" y="299" class="small">outer kicker post</text>
        <path class="member" d="M155 171 L190 132 L356 38 L385 77 L219 171 Z" />
        <text x="268" y="54" class="small">outer 4×6 rim</text>
        <path class="candidate" d="M113 171 L155 171 L190 132 L148 132 Z" />
        <text x="103" y="125" class="tiny">upper frame seat</text>
        <rect class="candidate" x="244" y="211" width="36" height="43" />
        <text x="283" y="235" class="tiny">lower post seat</text>
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="133" cy="155" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="133" cy="155" r="1.5" />
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="150" cy="166" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="150" cy="166" r="1.5" />
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="253" cy="223" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="253" cy="223" r="1.5" />
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="253" cy="240" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="253" cy="240" r="1.5" />
        <line class="bolt" x1="215" y1="142" x2="215" y2="254" /><path class="bolt" d="M210 247 L215 254 L220 247" />
        <text x="354" y="198" class="tiny">Z bolts; nut access below</text>
        <text x="75" y="249" class="small">Cross-bolts enter frame ↔ cleat</text>
        <!-- Center view -->
        <rect class="header" x="551" y="171" width="420" height="40" rx="2" />
        <rect class="ghost" x="551" y="171" width="76" height="40" />
        <text x="559" y="196">kicker header</text>
        <text x="555" y="224" class="tiny">front/top datums fixed · deepen rearward</text>
        <rect class="member" x="662" y="211" width="55" height="70" />
        <text x="635" y="299" class="small">center kicker post</text>
        <path class="member" d="M760 171 L797 141 L905 40 L936 76 L850 171 Z" />
        <text x="800" y="51" class="small">center 4×6 principal</text>
        <path class="candidate" d="M692 171 L760 171 L797 141 L729 141 Z" />
        <text x="753" y="133" class="tiny">full-section 4×6 block</text>
        <rect class="candidate" x="634" y="211" width="28" height="42" />
        <text x="626" y="268" class="tiny">separate post seat</text>
        <rect class="member" x="743" y="211" width="72" height="43" />
        <text x="731" y="269" class="tiny">center kicker backer</text>
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="779" cy="154" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="779" cy="154" r="1.5" />
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="793" cy="164" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="793" cy="164" r="1.5" />
        <text x="785" y="119" class="tiny">X pair through principal</text>
        <line class="bolt" x1="728" y1="141" x2="728" y2="212" /><path class="bolt" d="M723 205 L728 212 L733 205" />
        <text x="839" y="198" class="tiny">Z pair; nuts below header</text>
        <text x="557" y="248" class="small">Backer remains independent; its seat/access are unchanged</text>
      </svg>
    </figure>
    <div class="details">
      <p><strong>One joint grammar.</strong> Replace the outer three-piece knee detour with simple upper timber cleats beside the outer 4×6 rims and lower seats beside the kicker posts. At center, use one roughly 200 mm grain-length full-section 4×6 block beside each center principal; keep the center posts and kicker backers on distinct under-header seats.</p>
      <p><strong>Access to review.</strong> Cross-bolts pass through each frame member into its cleat (X or Y depends on station); vertical Z through-bolts tie each seat to the header, with nuts reached from below. Explore a single 2×10 or 2×12 header widened rearward while retaining the current front and top planes. The current 139.7 mm header depth does not establish a full block seat.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="concept" aria-labelledby="center-title">
    <div class="concept-head"><h2 id="center-title">3. Incremental option: enlarge only the upper center block</h2><span class="tag">Keeps the current outer knee while screening the center joint</span></div>
    <figure>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="center-svg-title center-svg-desc">
        <title id="center-svg-title">Center-only full-section block with outer knee retained</title>
        <desc id="center-svg-desc">The outer WJ03 knee assembly stays. At center, a roughly 200 millimeter full-section block replaces the short principal cleat and bolts to the center principal and the top of the header. The center post seat and kicker backer remain distinct below the header.</desc>
        <text x="35" y="25" font-weight="700">OUTER UNCHANGED</text>
        <text x="535" y="25" font-weight="700">CENTER PRINCIPAL / HEADER REVISED</text>
        <line class="section-divider" x1="500" y1="18" x2="500" y2="280" />
        <!-- Outer current reference -->
        <rect class="header" x="65" y="171" width="390" height="39" rx="2" />
        <text x="74" y="196">kicker header</text>
        <rect class="member" x="180" y="210" width="64" height="70" />
        <text x="162" y="296" class="small">outer kicker post</text>
        <path class="member" d="M155 171 L190 132 L356 38 L385 77 L219 171 Z" />
        <text x="274" y="55" class="small">outer 4×6 rim</text>
        <path class="existing-link" d="M208 162 L247 119" />
        <rect class="member" x="256" y="113" width="112" height="27" transform="rotate(-30 312 126.5)" />
        <rect class="member" x="105" y="145" width="111" height="25" />
        <rect class="member" x="248" y="210" width="118" height="28" />
        <text x="102" y="133" class="tiny">rear bridge</text>
        <text x="264" y="108" class="tiny">spine + under-header link</text>
        <text x="95" y="232" class="small">WJ03 outer 3-piece family remains</text>
        <!-- Center-only block -->
        <rect class="header" x="555" y="171" width="390" height="39" rx="2" />
        <rect class="ghost" x="555" y="171" width="390" height="39" />
        <text x="563" y="196">current header · 139.7 mm depth</text>
        <rect class="member" x="666" y="210" width="55" height="70" />
        <text x="638" y="296" class="small">center kicker post</text>
        <path class="member" d="M782 171 L819 143 L902 35 L933 71 L850 171 Z" />
        <text x="800" y="48" class="small">center 4×6 principal</text>
        <path class="candidate" d="M710 171 L782 171 L819 143 L747 143 Z" />
        <text x="754" y="124" class="tiny">≈200 mm full-section 4×6 block</text>
        <rect class="candidate" x="638" y="210" width="28" height="40" />
        <text x="629" y="264" class="tiny">post seat remains</text>
        <rect class="member" x="741" y="210" width="72" height="44" />
        <text x="727" y="271" class="tiny">separate center kicker backer</text>
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="769" cy="154" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="769" cy="154" r="1.5" />
        <circle class="bolt-head" cx="784" cy="164" r="4" /><circle class="bolt-dot" cx="784" cy="164" r="1.5" />
        <text x="776" y="113" class="tiny">X pair into principal</text>
        <line class="bolt" x1="747" y1="143" x2="747" y2="210" /><path class="bolt" d="M742 203 L747 210 L752 203" />
        <text x="839" y="199" class="tiny">Z pair into header</text>
        <line class="ghost" x1="710" y1="167" x2="782" y2="167" />
        <text x="837" y="156" class="tiny">seat fit to verify</text>
        <text x="558" y="246" class="small">Do not join the upper block to the lower post or backer</text>
      </svg>
    </figure>
    <div class="details">
      <p>The upper block follows the center principal grain and seats on the header top at Z=277 mm. The roughly 200 mm grain-length, full-section 4×6 block replaces the current 82 mm cleat. Two X-axis bolts tie it to the principal; two Z-axis bolts tie it to the header, with nuts below. The center kicker post ends at the header underside (Z=238.9 mm), so its joint remains separate below the header.</p>
      <p>This limited alternative leaves the current outer three-piece knee in place. The block footprint may exceed the current header depth; a deeper header or a fit/trim revision and full contact check may be required. The backer-to-header path remains separate.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>Owner-directed support move:</strong> raise the lowest rear support rail one 200 mm T-nut pitch in +T along the climbing surface while keeping the climbing and panel outlines fixed. Move its four lower-panel screw receivers with the rail and recheck their backing, edge support and load transfer. Preserve all 66 Hillman axes by count.</p>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 820 105" role="img" aria-labelledby="support-title support-desc">
      <title id="support-title">Owner-directed one-row raise of the lower rear support</title>
      <desc id="support-desc">The existing lowest rear support position is shown dashed. Its new position is one 200 millimeter T-nut pitch higher along the climbing surface, with the climbing outline fixed.</desc>
      <defs><marker id="support-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#173d55" /></marker></defs>
      <path class="ghost" d="M90 79 L680 28" />
      <text x="95" y="96" class="small">lowest rear support: existing station</text>
      <rect class="ghost" x="170" y="62" width="150" height="14" />
      <text x="177" y="73" class="tiny">existing rail</text>
      <line class="bolt" x1="390" y1="73" x2="390" y2="30" marker-end="url(#support-arrow)" />
      <text x="399" y="47" class="small">+T · 200 mm</text>
      <rect class="candidate" x="465" y="27" width="150" height="14" />
      <text x="470" y="23" class="tiny">raised rail: same panel outline</text>
    </svg>
    <p>The rail move is separate from the header joints above. The four fixed center-kicker screw axes into the backers remain a distinct receiver path. Do not count either screw group as a substitute for the bolted frame-member joints.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="open-items">
    <section>
      <h3>Geometry and access still to prove</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Exact block/header fit, full bearing footprint, grain orientation, shallow-seat depth and net sections.</li>
        <li>Receiver and washer support for each proposed X/Y and Z bolt; actual head/nut installation and underside wrench access.</li>
        <li>Effects of a deeper header and raised lower support on panel screw backing, neighboring joints, receiver cuts, transport and member replacement.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Load paths still to resolve</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Simultaneous actions through side/principal, post, cleat or block, header, and the rest of the frame under every adopted case.</li>
        <li>Wood bearing, bolt tension/shear/bending, contact opening, splitting and group/net-section checks at the complete joints.</li>
        <li>Header section and support response after any rearward depth change; no load share or resistance is assumed here.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <details class="concept">
    <summary>Technical source names and receiver axes</summary>
    <p>Outer reference: <code>knee_outer_*_spine</code>, <code>knee_outer_*_rear_bridge</code>, <code>knee_outer_*_under_header_link</code>, <code>base_side_left/right</code>, <code>base_post_outer_left/right</code>, and <code>base_header</code>.</p>
    <p>Center reference: <code>center_principal_cleat_left/right</code>, <code>center_post_cleat_left/right</code>, <code>base_principal_center_left/right</code>, <code>base_post_center_left/right</code>, <code>inner_kicker_backer_left/right</code>, and <code>base_header</code>.</p>
    <p>Raised support and current lower-panel axes: <code>base_rail_bottom_left/right</code>, <code>round_panel_lower_left_edge_1/2</code>, and <code>round_panel_lower_right_edge_1/2</code>.</p>
  </details>
  <p class="foot"><strong>Sketch key:</strong> grey-blue = existing timber; amber = proposed solid-timber seat/block; pale blue = panel/kicker reference; dashed line = exploratory extension or fit envelope. In the side elevation, X is through the page; Z is vertical. Bolt directions show intended geometry only, not proven access or a selected stack. No custom steel, inserts, half-laps, force result, or capacity is represented.</p>
</main>
